WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.068
-White House officials

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.270
are stonewalling
the impeachment inquiry

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.706
as Republicans shift
their defense of the president.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.741
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.977
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.114
We've established this
repeatedly,

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.215
but it's worth remembering

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.950
as the impeachment inquiry
intensifies.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.586
Donald Trump is very unpopular.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.122
He lost the popular vote in 2016

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.190
by a greater margin than
any president in history,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.292
and more people have had
a negative opinion of him

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.326
than a positive one

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.028
since virtually the start
of his campaign.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:32.098
No politician has been
this unpopular for this long

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.466
since Gerald Ford pardoned Nixon

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.202
and then fell down
that flight of stairs.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.372
Remember when we thought
slipping on wet stairs

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.740
was the dumbest thing
a president could do?

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.777
My God, we were adorable.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:46.345
Now, in Trump's defense,

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.615
he's not at risk
of slipping on wet stairs

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.350
because he keeps toilet paper
on his shoe

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.753
to dry each step as he goes.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.222
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.593
So Trump has always
been unpopular.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.062
By contrast, in 2018,
Democrats won the House

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.964
with the largest midterm margin
of all time,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.732
smashing the record
for the popular vote

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:07.733
in midterm elections.

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.202
In fact, that's the reason

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.270
this impeachment inquiry can
even happen in the first place.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.672
Democrats won an election,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.673
and now they have the power
to impeach the president.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:15.975
It's important to remember that

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.477
whenever you hear someone
call this an illegal coup

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:20.946
or when Republicans
say stuff like this.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.916
-You have to accept that
President Trump is president.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.250
That's the problem.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.154
They don't accept that President
Trump won the election.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.457
And America hates a sore loser

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.725
as much as any country
on the planet.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.562
This is an unfair process
being driven by sore losers.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.764
-They're sore losers?
They won the midterms.

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.833
You guys are the ones who,
whenever you lose,

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.768
pass a bunch of laws
making it harder to vote.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:44.804
That's why Republicans
love voter I.D.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.171
and gerrymandering so much.

00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:47.506
If they lose the next election,

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.075
they'll probably
introduce a bill

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.644
mandating that all voters must
have a valid driver's license

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.213
in at least
three different states

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.715
obtained at least six business
years prior to the election

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.417
and the only DMV in the country
is located in an abandoned hotel

00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.886
on a cliff in Yosemite

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.820
and it's open from 1:00 to 4:00
a.m. on alternate Wednesdays

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.556
in months beginning
with the letter "Q."

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:08.461
And -- And they're gonna call it
the Freedom to Vote Act.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.097
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.370
Trump's historic unpopularity
is clear.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.706
In the polling on impeachment,
as well, a majority of Americans

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.573
now say in polls that Trump
should be impeached.

00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:24.510
Now, you might expect
a president in that situation

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.479
to mount a defense and try
to change public opinion.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:30.249
Trump instead chooses to believe
that the polls are fake.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.718
-Mr. President, according to
several recent polls,

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.787
more Americans want you
to be impeached

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.423
and removed from office than the
number of Americans who don't.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.757
-You're reading the wrong polls.

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:41.627
-"Wall Street Journal,"
NBC, ABC, "Washington Post."

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:44.463
-I have the real polls.
I have the real polls.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.699
-Oh, you have the real polls.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.502
And they show that no one
wants you impeached

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.838
and you're keeping those polls
to yourself.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:52.839
Well, that makes sense.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.240
Trump seems like the kind of guy

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.942
who would keep good news
to himself.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.844
[ As Donald Trump ] "I mean,
these polls say people love me,

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.411
but bragging about it
just seems --

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:03.015
I don't know.
Is it, like, tacky?"

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.418
[ Normal voice ]
Trump will always be a low-rent
New York City con artist.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.820
He's like a guy with a table
outside the Nike store going,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.623
"Psst! Over here.
I got the real shoes."

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.559
And then he sells you a pair
of Air Gordons.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.793
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:17.830
So Trump deeply unpopular
in national polls,

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.365
and most Americans say
he should be impeached.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.566
The only thing he has
going for him

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.034
is that we still have a dumb,

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.936
antiquated
electoral college system

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.071
that lets like six states
decide the winner.

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:27.840
And Trump's unpopularity
is clear

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.742
whenever he steps
outside the bubble

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.076
of his rallies or Fox News,

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:33.546
like last weekend when he
got booed at the World Series.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.081
Now, you might be thinking,
"If the president

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.149
can't even to go a baseball game

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.584
without getting booed,
where can he go?"

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.619
And apparently his advisers
were wondering the same thing

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.789
because somebody thought surely
he can go to something like,

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.291
say, a UFC fight
without getting booed, right?

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.327
-Loud boos and some cheers
for the president.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.130
This is how he was received
at a UFC event last night

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.932
at Madison Square Garden
in New York.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.535
[ Crowd booing loudly ]

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:02.341
-Is that one of those
real polls he was talking about?

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.643
Even more embarrassing
for Trump,

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.478
the winner in one of
the UFC fights that night

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.646
posted a photo of himself
afterward with the caption,

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.549
"Bernie Sanders, you bastards."

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.383
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.818
I mean, the only way --

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:17.256
the only way this could have
been more embarrassing --

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.358
the only way it could have been
more embarrassing for Trump

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.060
is if Bernie himself
won the fight.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.862
[ As Bernie Sanders ]
"Put up your dukes.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:26.098
In the octagon, I'm the 1%."

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.067
[ Normal voice ]
The fact is, there's nowhere

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.570
Trump won't get booed,
save for his rallies.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.939
So the day before he got booed
at that UFC fight,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.441
Trump decided to bask in
the adoration of his crowds

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.709
at a rally in Mississippi.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.944
Now, these rallies
are such fawning affairs

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:40.846
that Trump routinely
makes up words

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.381
and no one seems to bat an eye,

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.984
which is exactly what happened
not once, but twice,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.185
at his rally on Friday.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.587
-First they engineered
the Russia hoax.

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:50.422
That was a total hoax.

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:53.625
The single greatest lies

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:57.897
ever foistered upon
the American people.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:03.168
It's all a phony deal,
this whole impeachment scam,

00:05:03.168 --> 00:05:08.140
to try to undermine
the 2020 election

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:13.712
and to de-legitimatize
one of the greatest elections.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:17.683
-Ah, yes, "foistered"
and "de-legitimatize."

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:20.018
Usually if you hear a loved one
talking like that,

00:05:20.018 --> 00:05:23.189
the next question you ask them
is, "Do you smell burnt toast?"

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.691
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.660
My favorite part
of Trump's made-up words

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.829
is how he ramps up to them
for effect with a long pause

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.565
and then gets them wrong.

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:35.000
It's like watching one
of those dudes run up to a pool

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.770
and do a cannonball
before realizing it's frozen.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.541
Aaah! Foistered again!

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.910
Putting aside the fake words,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.512
Trump's argument
fundamentally boils down

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.580
to accusing the Democrats,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.281
who won a record margin
in the midterms,

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:50.483
of trying to undo an election,

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.484
an argument he repeated later
at the rally

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:54.220
without any made-up words.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.555
-And then they figured
they could take us out

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.691
a different way,
very dishonestly, right,

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:02.661
with the lying and the spying
and the leaking.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.563
And we are kicking their ass.

00:06:04.563 --> 00:06:05.764
-Yeah, but you're not.

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.233
You see, they just passed
a resolution

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.567
on the impeachment inquiry,

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.502
and they've spent weeks
gathering damning testimony

00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:11.504
from direct witnesses.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:12.905
How are you kicking their ass?

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.274
Trump's like a football player
who does an end-zone dance

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.443
whenever the other team
scores a touchdown.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:20.379
"Patriots up 41-0, and it looks
like the Jets running back

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:23.349
is diving into the crowd.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.385
He's having fun."
Also, what's going on here?

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:28.653
-With the lying and the spying
and the leaking.

00:06:28.653 --> 00:06:29.688
-Is he working on his

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:31.590
Arnold Schwarzenegger
impression?

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.160
[ As Arnold Schwarzenegger ]
"With the lying, the spying
and leaking, impeaching,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.162
colluding and investigating
of the crimes,

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.797
things of that nature."

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.433
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.737
"The leaking and the creaking
and the peeping.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:48.040
And the peeking."

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.009
[ Normal voice ] So now
Democrats are moving forward

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.444
with the next phase
of their impeachment inquiry.

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:54.112
Today they began
releasing transcripts

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:56.181
of their depositions
with key witnesses.

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:58.384
And in response,
Trump has started suggesting

00:06:58.384 --> 00:07:00.619
that those transcripts
might somehow be fake.

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:01.753
Last night Trump attacked

00:07:01.753 --> 00:07:03.355
House Intelligence Chairman
Adam Schiff,

00:07:03.355 --> 00:07:05.558
tweeting that, "Schiff will
change the words that were said

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.792
to suit the Dems' purposes.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:08.627
Republicans should give
their own transcripts

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:09.795
of the interviews to contrast

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:11.363
with Schiff's
manipulated propaganda.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:14.266
He is a proven liar, leaker,
and freak."

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:16.536
Calling him a freak.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:18.971
You look like
a dollar-store action figure

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.841
called Mafia Goodfella.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.976
Trump keeps putting Republicans
in a bind

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:26.112
because he keeps insisting
that his infamous phone call

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:29.048
with the president of Ukraine
was not just unimpeachable,

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.216
but perfect.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.850
For example, yesterday
Trump spoke to reporters

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.985
and insisted yet again that
his phone call was perfect,

00:07:33.985 --> 00:07:37.256
although this time he put
a little extra flourish on it.

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:41.994
-The whistle-blower gave
a very inaccurate report

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.462
about my phone call.

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.664
My phone call was perfecto.

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:48.467
-It was perfecto.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.037
Sounds like a tourist trying
to fit in during a trip to Rome.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.472
[ Italian accent ]
"The phone call was perfecto!"

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:57.743
And now as a reward,
some pisghetti."

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.445
[ Normal voice ]
So Trump thinks his phone call

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:00.979
with the president of Ukraine
was perfect.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:02.682
Now, you'll recall that
in that conversation,

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.683
Trump tried to coerce
the president of Ukraine

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:06.419
to investigate Democrats
like Joe Biden

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:08.521
by telling him, "I would
like you to do us a favor."

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:09.621
And when he heard that,

00:08:09.621 --> 00:08:11.524
the president of Ukraine
was flustered,

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.825
or as Trump would put it...

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.059
-Foistered.

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:17.028
-So as Democrats start
releasing transcripts

00:08:17.028 --> 00:08:18.464
of their depositions,

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:19.798
the White House
is obviously desperate

00:08:19.798 --> 00:08:21.633
to do anything they can
to stop the process.

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:24.169
Today, for example,
four White House officials

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:26.739
refused to show up for
their scheduled hearings.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.541
-The witness list for today

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:31.611
appears to have gone
from four people to zero.

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:34.313
CNN has learned all four
White House officials

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:37.583
who were scheduled to testify
today will not be showing up.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:40.753
In fact, most of the witnesses
scheduled to testify this week

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:42.087
plan to stonewall.

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.789
-They're just refusing
to show up now.

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.024
How long before Trump
tries that tactic?

00:08:46.024 --> 00:08:47.159
The day he gets impeached,

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.894
he'll probably be holed up
in his bedroom

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:50.329
hiding under a pillow fort.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.131
[ As Donald Trump ] "You can't
impeach me if you can't find me.

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:54.399
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:57.769
And this is an invisible door."

00:08:57.769 --> 00:08:59.171
[ Normal voice ]
Trump and Republicans

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.039
keep changing their defense
because they don't have one.

00:09:01.039 --> 00:09:03.575
Democrats have now passed
a formal impeachment resolution.

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.010
And they're
releasing transcripts

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.145
of damning witness testimony.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.546
Trump's freaking out

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:09.949
as the impeachment inquiry
moves faster and faster and...

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:11.049
-Foistered.

00:09:11.049 --> 00:09:13.485
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:13.485 --> 00:09:15.521
[ Cheers and applause ]

